From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] main-loop: service browser event callbacks on the QEMU worker

With `PROXY_TO_PTHREAD`, Emscripten delivers DOM event callbacks to the QEMU
worker through its system proxy queue. QEMU's continuously running main loop
must poll that queue, otherwise a successful callback registration accepts
browser keys but never executes their QEMU-side handler.

Upstream baseline: QEMU v11.0.2 (e545d8bb7c3f).

---
 util/main-loop.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/util/main-loop.c b/util/main-loop.c
index 10dd2bf..0000000 100644
--- a/util/main-loop.c
+++ b/util/main-loop.c
@@ -35,5 +35,9 @@
 #include "qom/object.h"
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+#include <emscripten/proxying.h>
+#endif
+
 #ifndef _WIN32
 #include <sys/wait.h>
 #endif
@@ -572,6 +576,10 @@ void main_loop_wait(int nonblocking)
     int ret;
     int64_t timeout_ns;
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    emscripten_proxy_execute_queue(emscripten_proxy_get_system_queue());
+#endif
+
     if (nonblocking) {
         mlpoll.timeout = 0;
     }
